# quantum-os

> HTML shelf named quantum-os. Separate from Pieface.

## Purpose
Give a plain-language door to fitzyracing1/quantum-os.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Keep the original repo as the place for files.
2. Use this clone to explain the idea.
3. Send the reader to Pieface if they want that OS shelf.

## Key ideas
- quantum-os (the named shelf)
- HTML source

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/quantum-os
open_source()
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. open_source() → “go to fitzyracing1/quantum-os”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a reader wants Pie Face → Pieface
- If a reader wants this shelf → stay on the source

## What a person would notice
A named wrap on a quantum-os door.

